      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Leith Sugar House, founded in 1677, marked the town’s entry into the burgeoning sweet‑trade industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leith",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1750 the Edinburgh Roper & Sailcloth Co began in Leith, later expanding into wire ropes and cables.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leith",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After Cromwell’s 1650 victory, a Leith Citadel was erected in 1656 to regulate port traffic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leith",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Since 1907 the Leith Gala, now called Leith Festival Gala Day, has raised funds for local hospital beds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
